description:
Design a 3-to-8 decoder with an enable input. When the enable signal (EN) is high and the 3-bit input (ABC) represents a value from 1 to 7, the corresponding output line from the 8-bit output (Y) is set high; otherwise, all outputs are low. The decoder effectively converts the binary input into a unique active output line, allowing for signal routing in digital circuits.
module top_module(
    input [2:0] ABC,
    input EN,
    output reg [7:0] Y
);

code:
module top_module(
    input [2:0] ABC,
    input EN,
    output reg [7:0] Y
);always @ (ABC, EN) begin
        case ({ABC, EN})
            4'b0001: Y = 8'b00000001;
            4'b0010: Y = 8'b00000010;
            4'b0011: Y = 8'b00000100;
            4'b0100: Y = 8'b00001000;
            4'b0101: Y = 8'b00010000;
            4'b0110: Y = 8'b00100000;
            4'b0111: Y = 8'b01000000;
            default: Y = 8'b00000000;
        endcase
    end

endmodule

