description:
Implement a series of pipeline registers that store and propagate signal values through a multi-stage architecture. The module takes an n-bit wide input and provides an m-bit wide output, where the first output is the current value of the input, and the second output reflects the value after p clock cycles. The design employs a shift register mechanism, allowing the input to be captured and then sequentially passed through p registers on the rising edge of a clock signal, facilitating the staged processing of input data in a pipelined fashion suitable for high-speed systems.
module top_module(
  input clk,                // Add clk input
  input [n-1:0] in,
  output [m-1:0] out
);

code:
module top_module(
  input clk,                // Add clk input
  input [n-1:0] in,
  output [m-1:0] out
);parameter n = 4; // number of input signals
parameter m = 2; // number of output signals
parameter p = 3; // number of pipeline registers

reg [n-1:0] pipeline_reg [0:p-1];

assign out[0] = pipeline_reg[0][n-1:0];
assign out[1] = pipeline_reg[p-1][n-1:0];

integer i;

always @(posedge clk) begin
  pipeline_reg[0] <= in;
  for (i = 1; i < p; i = i + 1) begin
    pipeline_reg[i] <= pipeline_reg[i-1];
  end
end

endmodule

