Implement a Schmitt trigger circuit that provides hysteresis in the signal transition. It utilizes defined threshold voltage levels based on the percentage of the supply voltage (vdd) to determine its output state. When the input signal exceeds the rising threshold, the output is set to HIGH, while if it falls below the falling threshold, the output drops to LOW. This design helps mitigate noise and provides stable output for rapidly varying input signals.
