Develop a circuit that implements a complex multiplication operation based on predefined constants. The module takes a 32-bit input and processes it through various bitwise shifts and arithmetic operations to yield a 32-bit output, effectively performing a multiplication by a constant derived from hardcoded values. The output represents the result of multiplying the input by 10922 (an arithmetic combination of constants), achieving this through a series of wire calculations and assignments.
